# ===========================================================================
# .gitignore for the PDX depth-and-durability analysis
#
# Git reads a "#" only at the start of a line as a comment, so every comment
# below sits on its own line, never after a pattern.
# ===========================================================================


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Input data: never committed
#
# The Gao et al. (2015) workbook is 117 MB, above GitHub's 100 MB file
# limit. The Oberg et al. (2021) cohort was shared by its authors on request.
# The Project Data Sphere files are covered by a data use agreement that
# forbids redistribution. data/README.md says where each file comes from, so
# that file is the only thing under data/ that is tracked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/*
!data/README.md


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Restricted patient-level files, anywhere in the tree
#
# Section 14 of the analysis notebook writes two patient-level files for the
# figures notebook. They must stay on the computer that holds the Project
# Data Sphere data. These patterns stop them from being committed even if
# they are copied out of outputs/frozen/ or the rule in part 3 is relaxed.
# The SAS and transport formats are the formats Project Data Sphere releases.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/clinical_patients*
**/clinical_panel_restricted*
*.sas7bdat
*.sas7bcat
*.xpt


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Notebook outputs
#
# Committed: the results register, the run manifest and the result tables
# (outputs/results_register.*, outputs/manifest.json, outputs/tables/). They
# are small, they hold every reported number, and readers can check them
# against the paper without rerunning anything.
#
# Not committed: everything any run regenerates in bulk.
#   outputs/interim/   Parquet copies of the workbook sheets (Section 2.1)
#   outputs/frozen/    per-analysis records and figure data
#   outputs/figures/   figure files and the figure manifest
# To publish the figure data as well, delete the outputs/frozen/ line. Part 2
# still keeps the two patient-level files out.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
outputs/interim/
outputs/frozen/
outputs/figures/


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Jupyter
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.virtual_documents/
# Copies such as "Analysis_Notebook (1).ipynb" from repeated downloads
*\ (*).ipynb


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Local environments. The project environment is defined in environment.yml
# or requirements.txt and is built outside the repository.
.venv/
venv/
env/
.conda/


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6. Editors and operating systems
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# Windows
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# macOS
.DS_Store
._*

# Excel and Word lock files, created while a file is open
~$*
